      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nPD over MoRI breaks as soon as the prefill server runs a DSA model with PP > 1. MoRI registers the DSA indexer state without layer ids, and `build_transfer_entry_pairs` only falls back to positional pairing at PP = 1. A prefill stage has only its own layers while decode has all of them, so every state send fails with `PP-heterogeneous transfer requires layer ids on both peers`.\r\n\r\nSeen with GLM-5.2 on MI355X (prefill TP1 PP4, decode TP4).\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- `MoriKVManager._send_swa_dsa_state`: when DSA state has no layer ids and PP > 1, map each prefill stage onto the decode entries starting at its first layer via `get_mla_kv_ptrs_with_pp`, same as Mooncake. Raise before writing if decode doesn't have enough entries.\r\n- Skip this for hybrid linear+DSA pools (e.g. GLM-5-Next). Their DSA entries only cover full-attention layers, so slicing by model layer would pair the wrong layers.\r\n- Nothing else changes. The new path only runs in cases that used to raise.\r\n- Added `TestMoriPpDsaStatePairing`: checks the GLM-5.2 PP4 stage pairing, and that SWA without layer ids, a decode overrun and a hybrid pool all raise before any write.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nGLM-5.2 MXFP4, MoRI PD on MI355X: prefill TP1 PP4, decode TP4 + DP attention, MTP, HiCache.\r\nGSM8K with lm-eval 0.4.9.2, full test set (1319), 5-shot, greedy:\r\n\r\n| | exact_match |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| strict-match | 0.9697 ± 0.0047 |\r\n| flexible-extract | 0.9719 ± 0.0045 |\r\n\r\nNo before/after comparison since this setup didn't run at all before the fix. Measured on a v0.5.22 ROCm image with #28827 and the same pairing logic patched in.\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nN/A, the number and size of transfers don't change.\r\n\r\n\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41863118882](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41863118882)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41863118863](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41863118863)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41863118964](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41863118964)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
